0..76 Comment "// A peer still waiting when its counterpart abandons the rest is cancelled,"
77..119 Comment "// and the run answers its clause\'s value."
120..122 Comment "//"
123..197 Comment "// The abandoned rest held an end whose protocol had not ended, so it owed"
198..275 Comment "// its peer a cancellation. The peer\'s next action on its own end observes it"
276..324 Comment "// and abandons the peer\'s continuation in turn."
325..327 Comment "//"
328..402 Comment "// Each program below abandons its root\'s rest through an exit clause that"
403..478 Comment "// answers `7`. A peer parked at a receive is readied and abandoned, and an"
479..534 Comment "// end queued at an abandoned end is cancelled with it."
535..537 Comment "//"
538..578 Comment "// - see: #3305 — the cancellation hop"
579..650 Comment "// - see: Fowler, Lindley, Morris and Decova, _Exceptional Asynchronous"
651..728 Comment "//   Session Types_, POPL 2019, doi:10.1145/3290341 — cancellation reaching"
729..789 Comment "//   the peer and every end left in a cancelled end\'s buffer"
791..864 Comment "/// The peer sends, then waits on a payload the abandoned rest would have"
865..874 Comment "/// sent."
